@startuml
title Platform use cases (as implemented + planned)
left to right direction

actor "Operator" as Operator
actor "Drone" as Drone
actor "Backend timer" as Timer

rectangle "Drone Drive-Test Platform" {
  usecase "Navigate administrative geography" as Navigate
  usecase "Search location (preview / commit)" as Search

  usecase "Create draft mission" as Draft
  usecase "Draw / modify / translate route" as Route
  usecase "Set name, drone, schedule" as Schedule
  usecase "Plan mission (DRAFT -> PLANNED)" as Plan
  usecase "Cancel mission" as Cancel
  usecase "Derive new draft from failed mission" as Derive

  usecase "Review mission result" as Review
  usecase "Select / approve / reject measurements" as Decide
  usecase "Save result revision" as Save
  usecase "Finalize result revision" as Finalize

  usecase "Explore Signal Quality heatmap" as Explore
  usecase "Refresh heatmap version" as Refresh
  usecase "Edit heatmap palette" as Palette

  usecase "Claim planned mission" as Claim
  usecase "Report execution status" as Report
  usecase "Upload mission result" as Upload
  usecase "Fail missed-dispatch missions" as Sweep

  usecase "Monitor drone status (planned)" as Monitor
}

Operator --> Navigate
Operator --> Search
Operator --> Draft
Operator --> Plan
Operator --> Cancel
Operator --> Derive
Operator --> Review
Operator --> Explore
Operator --> Monitor

Drone --> Claim
Drone --> Report
Drone --> Upload
Timer --> Sweep

Draft ..> Route : <<include>>
Draft ..> Schedule : <<include>>
Review ..> Decide : <<include>>
Save ..> Review : <<extend>>
Finalize ..> Save : <<extend>>
Refresh ..> Explore : <<extend>>
Palette ..> Explore : <<extend>>
Search ..> Navigate : <<extend>>

note right of Monitor
  Not implemented. Today the operator only
  sees the mission state badge in the
  Missions list; there is no live drone view
  (see docs/future-features.md).
end note

note bottom of Finalize
  Finalizing does not push anything to the
  heatmap. The operator gets a fading advisory
  and refreshes the heatmap manually
  (ADR-0011).
end note
@enduml
